WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.900
Right now, I want

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.102
to talk about how we got here

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.802
and what is going on

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.671
and what we can expect going forward.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.239
I want to bring in now our senior

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.475
legal affairs correspondent, Paula Reid.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.909
She has been following this

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.044
from the very beginning.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:11.911
Good morning to you.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.513
What are you learning about

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.547
still the indictment

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.849
and what we have to go through?

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.451
And it is still yet to be unsealed.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.419
It's amazing

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:19.953
even the former

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.021
president's attorneys

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.256
still don't know the charges

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.991
that he has been

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.726
that have been filed under seal.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.060
Now, that's

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.061
because they want to treat him

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:28.795
the same way

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.897
they would treat any other defendant.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.832
And what we're expected to see on Tuesday

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.434
is that he will go before a judge.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.902
He will be fingerprinted.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.704
He will be photographed again.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.639
They want this to be like any other case.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.006
But, Don,

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.241
we know this is

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.176
unlike any other case in U.S. history.

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.479
A Manhattan grand

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.048
jury voting to indict

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.049
former President

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.850
Donald Trump Thursday

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.886
while the case is still under seal.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:53.453
Sources

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.421
tell CNN

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.723
he faces more than 30 counts

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.725
related to business fraud.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.293
The former president responding

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.261
to the indictment

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.195
calling the Manhattan

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.029
district attorney

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.065
Alvin Bragg, a disgrace.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:05.765
And claiming

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.501
the entire investigation is a witch hunt.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.669
He's ready to fight.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.703
You know, he's the toughest guy

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.671
I know yet.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.338
And

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:14.774
he was shocked

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.443
you know, because we really were

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.077
I was shocked

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.778
today, the rule of law

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.480
in the United States of America died.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.247
The indictment

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.416
concludes a yearslong probe

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.652
investigating a hush money payment

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.054
to adult film star Stormy Daniels

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:31.091
to remain silent about an alleged affair

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.025
with Trump.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.892
An affair.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:36.196
Trump denies the case relies in part

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.031
on the testimony of Trump's former

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.265
personal attorney,

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.500
Michael Cohen,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.068
who has in the past

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:45.238
pleaded guilty to nine federal crimes,

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.639
including lying.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.907
I am a convicted felon

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.009
and I am a disbarred lawyer, but

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.544
I also brought the documents.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:53.546
There's plenty

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.682
of testimony and corroborating testimony

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:56.850
to go around.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.954
Cohen paid Daniels $130,000

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.323
just weeks before the 2016

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.024
presidential election,

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.693
according to court filings.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.662
The Trump Organization reimbursed Cohen

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.832
$420,000.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:15.001
It's a fight against his

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.302
rejection of truth

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.571
and his manufacturing of stories

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.374
that really motivated her.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.308
The Manhattan

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.643
District Attorney's Office

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.411
was also asking questions

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.280
during the grand jury proceedings

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.449
about Karen McDougal.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:32.852
She was paid $150,000

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:33.653
by the company

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.655
that publishes the National Enquirer

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:36.956
to stay silent

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.125
about another alleged affair with Trump.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.894
Trump has denied

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.829
any affair with McDougal.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.097
Trump's longtime friend

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:44.998
and then chairman

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.299
of the National Enquirer's

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.167
parent company,

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.902
David Pecker, is believed

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.770
to have orchestrated the payment

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.772
and was one of the last witnesses

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.308
to testify before the grand jury Monday.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.343
But even Trump's potential

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.345
Republican presidential rivals

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.581
criticizing the indictment.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.516
Governor Ron DeSantis tweeting

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.984
it's un-American.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.452
And Trump's former vice

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.954
president Mike Pence,

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.255
telling CNN,

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.424
I think the unprecedented indictment

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.293
of a former president

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.294
of the United States

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:16.563
on a campaign finance issue

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.431
is an outrage.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:20.733
And one of the former

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.768
president's attorneys,

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.002
it tells me that the district

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:23.736
attorney actually

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.672
wanted him to surrender today.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:26.506
That would have been

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.074
a really tight turnaround

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.709
considering all the security

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.010
that they would need to get in place.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.278
They wanted to tamp down the circus

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.913
like atmosphere that is sure to follow.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.114
So they want it instead of waiting

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.016
till Tuesday over the weekend.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.918
Time for people to gather and so forth.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.320
They wanted him to turn himself in

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.821
so that this can be over and done

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.156
with at least the appearance

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:43.890
so much for that.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.425
We'll see him on Tuesday write

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.360
in what will surely be a circus

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.561
like atmosphere. All right.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.996
Thank you very much, Paul Reed.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.532
We'll continue to follow this, Caitlin.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:52.632
Well,

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.733
I think it's important this morning

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.269
to step back and look at how we got here.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.870
This didn't just come out of nowhere

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.672
and it was back in 2006, actually,

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.173
that Trump

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:00.873
first met

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.810
both Stormy Daniels and Karen McDougal.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:04.844
Five years after

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:06.346
that is when Stormy Daniels tried

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.480
to sell her story

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.515
to a publication known as Life in Style.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.352
But Michael Cohen then working for Trump

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.553
started a lawsuit

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.388
and the story was never published.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.257
Fast forward to 2015.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.024
Trump announces

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.659
that he's running for president.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:20.960
Of course, he came down the escalator

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.961
at Trump Tower

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.029
the following spring

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.464
that Daniels tries to sell her

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.832
story again.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.799
No one bites.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.735
Not even the National Enquirer

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:29.469
that summer.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.771
Karen McDougal story is caught and killed

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:32.438
And remember,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.540
CNN obtained a secret audio tape

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.809
at the time of Trump and Cohen discussing

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.311
how all of it would play out.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.279
You hear the mention,

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:40.913
David, as in David

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.782
Pecker of The National Enquirer,

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.117
who also testified this week

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.318
before the grand jury.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.219
And Alan,

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:46.786
that's Allen

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.821
Weisselberg, who was the CFO of the Trump

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:49.856
Organization.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:50.857
Is right now

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.458
still serving a jail sentence

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.163
I need to open up a company

00:04:57.497 --> 00:05:00.566
for the transfer of all of that info

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.235
regarding my friend David.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.070
So I'm I'm all over that

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.471
and I spoke to Allen about it.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.240
When it comes time for the financing,

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.941
which will be sure to

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.110
wash my hands and we'll have to

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:11.844
pay this off.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.413
Okay. Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:16.082
I got it. No, no, no.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.151
A few months after that conversation is

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.986
what a bombshell dropped in the Access

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.322
Hollywood published a tape of former

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.589
President Trump

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.191
candidate Trump at the time.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.794
The very next day on October 8th, is

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.529
when Daniels seemed to sense

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:32.031
there was opportunity to pitch her story

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.099
once again.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:35.435
After years of failing to sell it.

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:37.603
This time there was interest.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:38.771
On October 10th,

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:39.639
three days

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.341
after the Access Hollywood tape,

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.108
and about a month

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.710
before the presidential election,

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.211
Michael Cohen agreed to pay

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.079
Stormy Daniels

00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:49.282
$130,000 in exchange for her silence.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.084
That deal threatened Daniels

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:51.684
with severe

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.652
financial penalties

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.820
if she ever spoke

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.422
about the alleged affair on the 28th.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.024
That agreement was signed

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.159
11 days before Election Day.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.294
Of course, an election

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.296
we now all know Trump won.

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.398
Poppy, all of this is is the heart

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.133
of what the district attorney

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.201
is now looking at,

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.335
what they are going into.

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:10.336
It is remarkable

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:12.305
the time that has lapsed here

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:13.773
and the fact that it has culminated

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:14.574
with this indictment

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:17.276
that we saw to walk through from 2006

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:18.344
until where we were

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.946
and where we are now is remarkable.

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:20.880
And Caitlin, thank you.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.682
So that's the timeline.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:23.082
Let's talk about

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:24.517
what came immediately after. Right.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.686
20, 16, 20, 17.

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:29.055
Donald Trump paid Michael Cohen back

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.556
with a series of monthly

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:31.691
checks right

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.793
$35,000 a month, month

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.762
after month, different case.

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:36.829
But when Michael Cohen

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:37.964
was looking at charges,

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:40.199
the DOJ said that those checks

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.602
were accounted for as legal expenses,

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:43.636
even though they were not

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:44.971
part of any legal service

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.140
that he provided to Trump that year.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.241
So now what?

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.343
Hoenig is back are CNN senior

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:51.377
legal analyst okay.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:52.044
Ali,

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.781
let's start, I guess, where we are now,

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.848
where we'll be on Tuesday.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.150
What happens now?

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.384
So this is historic.

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:59.485
This is unprecedented.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.052
But you know what?

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.854
It's just a case as well.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:02.889
It will be titled

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:04.624
People of the State of New York

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:05.958
versus Donald Trump.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.627
So what are we going to see on Tuesday?

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:08.928
This is what we call an arraignment.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.530
It's a first appearance in court.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:10.997
Donald Trump

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.298
will be, in all likelihood,

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:13.166
fingerprinted.

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:15.201
He may have his mug shot taken as well.

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:15.868
Mug shots,

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:16.235
by the way,

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:17.637
are typically not available

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:19.705
to the public under New York state law.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:20.706
At that proceeding,

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:22.074
the indictment will be unsealed.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.376
That's when we'll see.

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:23.643
That's

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.111
when we'll know what the charges are.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.379
The judge will read the charges

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:27.046
to Donald Trump,

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:28.448
ask him to enter his plea.

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:30.216
He will certainly plead not guilty.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.384
And then the judge will almost

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:32.852
certainly release Donald Trump

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.720
and what we call his own recognizance,

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.822
meaning come back when you will.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.489
One important thing

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:37.857
I want to notice this court,

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.358
what we're going to be is a state court.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.360
It is called somewhat confusingly,

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.062
New York Supreme Court.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:44.130
You hear Supreme Court.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.932
You think of nine justices in robes.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:46.933
The Supreme Court here

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.968
means the trial level court

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.269
in downtown Manhattan

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.270
After that arraignment,

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.639
we're going to be into the trial process.

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:54.941
We're going to have motions

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:56.175
watch for Donald Trump's team

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:57.777
to ask to downgrade or dismiss

00:07:57.777 --> 00:07:58.744
some of the charges.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:00.246
Then Discovery prosecutor

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:01.180
will have to turn over

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.381
all their evidence,

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.350
good and bad to the defense.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.751
And we will get to a trial.

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:06.786
If there's a conviction,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.154
we will get to sentencing

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.789
and then it's all got to go up on appeal.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:11.090
So we are at the very beginning

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.992
and beginning of a very long process.

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.560
Let's talk about potential charges here.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.028
John Miller broke the news last night.

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:17.897
This indictment has 30 plus counts.

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:18.831
What could they be?

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:20.533
Yeah, so we know that there's over

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:21.367
30 counts

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:23.102
that doesn't necessarily correlate

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:24.370
with seriousness.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.771
But let's take a look at what it could be

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.540
if these charges are based on the hush

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.140
money payments

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.408
